  "title": "Tuna and pepper Tapenade",
  "description": null,
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Between the terrine and the dip, this tuna and pepper Tapenade is perfect as an aperitif for dipping celery stalks or carrot sticks, grilled toast...</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":27350,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1733386382945} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 27350-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Tuna and pepper Tapenade</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_1337.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\t\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>160 g canned tuna ((drained))</li><li>1/2 red pepper</li><li>1/2 yellow pepper</li><li>150  g cream cheese (Philadelphia style)       </li><li>Salt and black pepper</li><li>Few drops Tabasco™ ((optional))</li><li>A bit chopped parsley</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li><p>With a fork, work the tuna and cheese in a bowl.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_1305.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Cut the pepper in half lengthwise. Remove the seeds and filaments.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_1306.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Cut the peppers into small cubes and add them to the bowl. Add salt, pepper and mix well.</p><p>If you want a spicier tapenade, add a few drops of Tabasco™.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_1309.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Cover with plastic wrap and refrigerate for an half hour.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_1311.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Sprinkle with chopped parsley and serve.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_1323.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol><h4>For a nice presentation:</h4><ol><li><p>Line small bowls with cellophane. Fill with the tuna terrine and pack well into the bowl.</p><p>Invert onto a serving plate and remove the bowl (and cellophane!) to obtain a small dome. Decorate as you wish.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/IMG_1337.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Apéritifs</div><div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-cuisine\">française</div><div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-keyword\">Terrine au saumon fume, Terrine au thon</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
